WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.850
I have tinnitus.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.550
I have tinnitus.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:07.850
I have tinnitus.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.090
I have tinnitus in one ear.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.350
I have tinnitus.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.690
I have tinnitus.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.900
Welcome to the Coping
with Tinnitus Course.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.500
First, what is the right
way to say tinnitus?

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.040
Some people say tinnitus,
while other people say tinnitus.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.600
You can pronounce it either way.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.100
In this course, we will say tinnitus
with the accent on the first syllable.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.300
This course contains seven sections.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.840
This section is a brief introduction
to the content of this course.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.884
We will go over several
issues, a disclaimer,

00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:52.238
advice when to seek medical treatment,
and a description about

00:00:52.278 --> 00:00:57.380
the one coping assessment instrument
that we use in this course.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.613
We will describe data
collection in the course

00:00:59.653 --> 00:01:02.880
and your rights to opt out
of the coping assessment.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.460
Section 2 contains audiological
tips related to tinnitus.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.780
Section 3 discusses stress and how
to analyze the type of stress you are facing.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.520
Sections 4 through 6
are about coping strategies.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.560
Section 4 covers problem-solving coping.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.000
Section 5 discusses
stress management coping.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.760
Section 6 describes social support coping.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.052
Section 7 contains a summary
of the content as well as additional

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:37.160
coping strategies that can be used
when facing unremitting stress.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.520
The disclaimer is the following.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.780
This course does not give specific
medical advice to individuals.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.687
The content provides information
about tinnitus to help

00:01:51.727 --> 00:01:55.360
you better understand
options for living with it.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:02.320
Each person should seek medical advice,
diagnosis, and or treatment by a physician.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:08.878
A medical doctor can examine you and take
your medical history in order to screen

00:02:08.918 --> 00:02:14.860
for possible medical issues that may
be related to some forms of tinnitus.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.178
The next few slides will
provide some guidance about when

00:02:19.218 --> 00:02:24.780
and how soon you should seek
medical care when you have tinnitus.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.480
Here are tips about when you should seek
medical care in the context of tinnitus.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:40.140
Seek help from a physician immediately
if you experience any of the following.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.160
Trauma to the head
or neck or bodily injury.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:49.380
Hearing loss in one or both ears
that is sudden and unexplained.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.440
Paralysis or weakness
of any facial muscles.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:59.960
Also, if you experience any of the following,
seek help from an ENT,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.200
ear, nose, and throat clinic,
or a physician as soon as possible.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.960
Your tinnitus symptoms pulse
with the beat of your heart.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.157
You have ear pain
or drainage from your ear,

00:03:13.197 --> 00:03:19.360
a possible sign of infection,
or you have vertigo or spinning dizziness.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:27.113
If you notice any significant change
in hearing, tinnitus, or ear related issues,

00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:33.810
ask your primary care provider for a referral
in the near future to an audiologist.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:39.530
An audiologist is a non-physician
hearing health care provider or an ear,

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.470
nose, and throat ENT specialist.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.965
If you experience extreme
anxiety, depression,

00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:50.395
or a current plan to end
your life and have a way to do it,

00:03:50.435 --> 00:03:56.330
please immediately go to emergency
care or to a mental health clinic.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:03.652
Regarding surgery, please note
that most types of tinnitus are related

00:04:03.692 --> 00:04:09.070
to issues with nerves, that is to say
related to some kind of nerve damage.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:13.870
For these types of tinnitus,
surgery is not an option.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.686
In rare cases, some muscular spasms,
constricted blood vessels,

00:04:18.726 --> 00:04:24.370
or metabolic conditions can cause
what is called objective tinnitus.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.310
Sometimes surgery can help
to treat this kind of tinnitus.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.805
In other kinds of rare
cases of tinnitus, a tumor,

00:04:31.845 --> 00:04:35.570
often benign, can impinge
on the hearing nerve.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.066
When this happens,
the tinnitus usually occurs in one

00:04:39.106 --> 00:04:44.010
ear and appears slowly
with hearing loss in the same ear.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.970
These kinds of tumors can
be removed with surgery.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.340
The most common kind of tinnitus
is called subjective tinnitus.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.460
It is a symptom of neural damage.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:05.400
At the present time, there is no consistent
method of curing this kind of tinnitus.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.782
But, as medical science
advances in many areas,

00:05:08.822 --> 00:05:14.360
it is possible that a way to repair
the damaged nerve will be discovered.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:19.603
Section 2 will go into more details
about the possible causes of tinnitus,

00:05:19.643 --> 00:05:23.275
as well as some modifications
that you can do in order

00:05:23.315 --> 00:05:27.400
to decrease how much you
are aware of your tinnitus.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.020
This course will start
with a scale called the Brief COPE.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.480
It is a widely used scale
to assess people's coping.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.880
This course will end with the same scale.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.475
You can use those numbers
to understand whether your use

00:05:45.515 --> 00:05:50.160
of coping strategies has altered
after going through this course.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.446
Now, let us get started with Section 2,

00:05:55.486 --> 00:06:01.600
which will go into more details about
the audiological aspects of tinnitus.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.860
Welcome to the coping
with tinnitus course.
